{
  "name": "Schrödinger Onsager clusters: random start",
  "description": "Defocusing Schrödinger (a superfluid in a box): 64 vortices, 32 of each sign, scattered at random. Close opposite pairs find each other and annihilate in bursts of sound; losing those low-energy pairs leaves the survivors with more energy each (\"evaporative heating\"), and like-sign vortices start to gather into clusters, as Onsager predicted. Slower and less tidy than the shear layer: give it time (measured: 64 vortices fall to 14 by 80k steps, while the share with a same-sign nearest neighbour climbs from 0.42 to 0.71). Tip: Display → mode → reagent + param outlines shows the box walls.",
